course: dictionary
lesson: 10452
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. The word trust is a good example. It can mean to believe someone is honest and good, or to believe something is true or will work.
explain: «Wait for trusted news before believing or sharing that a famous person has died.» Here trusted means reliable, from a source you can believe. The clue is that a shocking post on no trusted news site is probably fake, so trusted news is news you can rely on.
explain: «Leaving a group can feel scary, but trusted adults can help.» Here trusted adults means grown-ups you can believe in and go to for help, such as parents, teachers and police. Test your meaning by putting it in the sentence: "adults you can believe in can help" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Trust (verb) means to believe someone is honest and good, or to believe something is true or will work.
fact: Trust (noun) is the feeling of believing in someone.
fact: «Trusted» describes someone or something you can rely on, like «trusted news» or «a trusted adult».
fact: A trust is also an organisation that looks after money or property for others.
fact: Useful phrases include «trust me», «break someone's trust», «trust your instincts» and «trust in».
exercise: «Wait for trusted news before believing or sharing that a famous person has died.» In this sentence, what does trusted mean? | *Reliable, from a source you can believe | Loud and shouting | Very old and worn out | Quick and easy to find
exercise: «If you think a friend has stolen something, you have a duty to act, starting by talking to them or a trusted adult.» Who is a trusted adult? | A stranger who asks for your secrets | *A grown-up you can believe in and go to for help | A shop worker who sells sweets | Any adult you have never met
exercise: Jayden says «I trust the map». What does trust mean here? | *Believes it is true and will work | Is afraid of the map | Hides the map from everyone | Believes the map is honest and kind
test: Trust (noun) means: | *The feeling of believing in someone | A kind of bank account for children | A rope pulled hard in a game | A map that shows the way home
test: «Headlines are written to grab you, so read the story underneath.» What should you do before believing a shocking post? | Believe it because it is shocking | *Check that the story is on a trusted news site | Share it quickly before anyone else sees it | Ignore all news forever
exam: Which sentence uses trust as a verb? | *Trust your instincts when something feels wrong | Her trust in him was broken | A feeling of trust grew between them | The trust looks after the money for the children
